{
  "contract": "memory-http",
  "version": 1,
  "canonicalSchema": 2,
  "description": [
    "Golden payloads for the canonical memory HTTP surface.",
    "",
    "This file is the frozen data boundary. Both the Python handler and the Kotlin RemoteMemoryGateway",
    "read it, so the wire format is verified on both sides instead of assumed to agree.",
    "",
    "The record shape is a one-to-one projection of CanonicalMemory using the field names, enum",
    "spellings and instant formatting that canonical-memory-v2.json already uses. It is not a third",
    "memory schema: nothing is invented, nothing is dropped, and no field is renamed.",
    "",
    "Two version numbers are in play and are not the same thing: `version` here names the HTTP surface,",
    "`canonicalSchema` names the semantic contract it carries.",
    "",
    "Instants on the wire are always canonical UTC (`...Z`). The `normalization` case pins that a client",
    "or server receiving an offset form re-emits the canonical one, so the same moment never has two",
    "spellings on the wire."
  ],
